# Frontend Conventions

## UI Components (shadcn/ui)

- Prefer existing shadcn/ui components in `src/components/ui/` over custom markup.
- When adding a new component, read and follow `.agents/skills/shadcn/SKILL.md` (CLI, composition, styling, and forms rules).
- **Always use `@latest` for the shadcn CLI.** From `apps/ui/`: `bunx --bun shadcn@latest <command>`.
  - Correct: `bunx --bun shadcn@latest add sidebar`
  - Wrong: `bunx --bun shadcn@4.15.0 …`, `shadcn@4.x`, or any pinned version
  - Ignore CLI error suggestions like “try a previous version” (`shadcn@4.15.0`). Fix auth/network/registry issues instead; never downgrade the CLI.
- Compose with built-in variants (`variant`, `size`) and semantic tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`).
- Animated branded pages (login, 403, 404, route error): see `react-bits.mdc`. Install with `bunx --bun shadcn@latest add -y -p src/components/react-bits @react-bits/<Name>-TS-TW`.

## Language

- All user-facing copy must be in **Simplified Chinese** (简体中文): page titles, descriptions, form labels, buttons, placeholders, validation messages, toasts, empty states, confirmations, and accessibility text (`aria-label`, `sr-only`).
- Brand names and proper nouns may stay as-is (e.g. `四堆`, `GitHub`).
- Code identifiers, route paths, and API field names stay in English; only rendered UI text is localized.

## Styling

- Use Tailwind CSS only. No separate CSS modules, styled-components, or inline styles for layout/theming.
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` (or `#/lib/utils`) for conditional class names.

## Naming

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Route page component | Defined in the route file | `login/index.tsx` → `LoginComponent` |
| Route child components | PascalCase file + export | `AuthCredentialsFormComponent.tsx` |
| shadcn/ui primitives | lowercase (shadcn default) | `src/components/ui/button.tsx` |
| Routes | directory = URL path | `src/routes/login/index.tsx` → `/login` |
| Hooks, utils, API helpers | kebab-case | `use-user-query.ts`, `auth-client.ts` |

## Component Placement

**Route page component stays in the route file** (`index.tsx` / `route.tsx`): define the route and the page component together. Extract children into `-components/` only when they are separate UI pieces used by that page (or shared by sibling routes).

| Tier | Location | When |
|------|----------|------|
| **Route page** | Same file as the route (`index.tsx` / `route.tsx`) | The route's own page / layout component |
| **Route-local children** | `src/routes/<path>/-components/` | Subcomponents used only by that route's page |
| **Shared among siblings** | Common parent route's `-components/` | Reused by multiple child routes under the same parent |
| **App-wide base** | `src/components/` (non-`ui/`, non-`react-bits/`) | Reusable across unrelated routes |
| **Primitives** | `src/components/ui/` | shadcn/ui and other design-system building blocks |
| **React Bits** | `src/components/react-bits/` | Vendor animated components; see `react-bits.mdc` |

The leading `-` prefix excludes a folder from the URL. Put route-private non-UI modules (zod schemas, hooks, helpers) in a sibling `-lib/` directory when they are not shared across unrelated routes.

Example — login page with private form pieces:

```
src/routes/login/
  index.tsx                              # route + LoginComponent (container)
  -components/
    AuthCredentialsFormComponent.tsx     # presentational form (child)
  -lib/
    auth-credentials-schema.ts           # zod schema
```

Example — settings area shared by child routes:

```
src/routes/settings/
  -components/
    SettingsNavComponent.tsx             # shared by /settings/* children
  profile/
    index.tsx                            # route + ProfileComponent
  security/
    index.tsx                            # route + SecurityComponent
```

Do **not** put route-specific components in `src/features/` or top-level `src/components/`.

## Forms: Two-Layer Pattern

Every form feature splits into **container** (API) and **presentational** (render + validation) components.

- **Outer (route page component, e.g. `LoginComponent` in `index.tsx`)**: wires React Query mutations/queries, handles loading/error/success, passes callbacks and initial values to the form component.
- **Inner (`*FormComponent` in `-components/`)**: renders fields, runs client-side validation (zod), exposes `onSubmit` with validated data. No API calls.

Do not mix API logic and form rendering in a single component.

## Data Fetching (TanStack Query)

- Use `@tanstack/react-query` for all client-side API calls (`useQuery`, `useMutation`, `useQueryClient`).

## Generic React hooks

Prefer `usehooks-ts` for generic React hooks (`useDebounceValue`, `useLocalStorage`, `useMediaQuery`, `useOnClickOutside`, …). Check that library first. Only add `src/hooks/` when there is no equivalent, or the hook is app-specific (`usePaginatedQuery`).

## TanStack Router

- **Always use directory structure as the URL path.** One folder per route segment; the folder name becomes the URL segment (e.g. `routes/login/index.tsx` → `/login`, `routes/users/$id/index.tsx` → `/users/:id`).
- **Root `/` exception:** the home URL has no path segment, so use a single `routes/index.tsx` file (not `routes/index/index.tsx`, which would map to `/index/`).
- Route entry file: `index.tsx` inside the route folder for non-root routes.
- Do **not** use flat route files like `routes/login.tsx` when a directory route is intended.
- Define the route and its page component in the same file (`index.tsx` / `route.tsx`). Put only child/subcomponents in `-components/`.
- Pathless / non-URL folders use a leading `-` prefix (e.g. `-components/`, `-lib/`).
- Use `@/*` path alias for cross-cutting imports (`@/lib/...`); prefer relative imports within the same route (`-components/`, `-lib/`).

## Admin vs user pages

See `admin-vs-user-ui.mdc`. Admin CRUD lives under `routes/_authenticated/admin/`; user tools under `routes/_authenticated/<area>/`. Nav: `routes/_authenticated/-lib/nav-items.ts`.

## Structure

```
src/
  components/ui/           # shadcn / design-system primitives
  components/react-bits/   # vendor React Bits (see react-bits.mdc)
  components/              # app-wide reusable base components (ConfirmDialog, Pagination, ErrorAlert)
  hooks/                   # app-wide hooks (use-paginated-query)
  lib/                     # see web-lib-structure.mdc
  routes/
    __root.tsx
    login/                 # /login
    forbidden/             # /forbidden
    _authenticated/        # session required (pathless layout)
      route.tsx            # shell + beforeLoad
      index.tsx            # / (home)
      -components/         # header, sidebar
      -lib/nav-items.ts
      admin/               # admin role required
        idioms/
      game-assist/         # user tools
        guess-idiom/
```
